# Environment variables only when two runtimes need them

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L1 configuration.

## Use This When

- Code needs a value that might differ between machines or environments.

## Stop Here If

- The value is a fixed contract (keep it in code as a constant) or it is read by at least two runtimes and declared once.

## Core rule

- Add an environment variable only when at least two runtimes read it or it truly differs per environment; otherwise it is a constant in code.
- Parse environment once at startup with a Zod schema; the rest of the code receives typed values.
- Every variable a turbo task reads is declared in `turbo.json` (`globalPassThroughEnv` or the task's `env`); turbo strips undeclared variables silently.
